Coach: You could know all your numbers, but if you don't trust your swing, or trust the distances, or trust yourself, like…

168
00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:36.660
Coach: you know, I don't know, I am a big mental code.

169
00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.660
Natalie Spiska: Can you hear me? I can't hear you right now.

170
00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:02.260
Natalie Spiska: Hello?

171
00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.340
Natalie Spiska: I can't hear you, can you hear me?

172
00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.940
Natalie Spiska: Okay. I don't think I can hear you, unfortunately.

173
00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.380
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, I still can't hear you.

174
00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:52.809
Natalie Spiska: Maybe, try leaving and reconnecting again?

175
00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:25.710
Coach: Hello?

176
00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:26.580
Natalie Spiska: Oh, I can hear you now.

177
00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:31.259
Coach: That better, sir. I had a phone call come in, I don't know how I can turn that off, but…

178
00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:32.960
Coach: Oh, they're hot.

179
00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:37.719
Natalie Spiska: That's all good. I only have, two more questions left anyways, so…

180
00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.520
Coach: Perfect.

181
00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:46.559
Natalie Spiska: What role do you see technology playing in collegiate golf in, like, in the future, and do you think it'll change the recruiting process in any way?

182
00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:53.919
Coach: Yeah, I mean, I think… I think data's always getting better, and…

183
00:18:55.680 --> 00:19:04.519
Coach: I mean, even, I don't know if you've even looked at… I don't know how much it's technology, but, like, at that golf performance down in [City], I don't know if the coach has taken you there, they have that PDI stuff.

184
00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:05.550
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

185
00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:10.359
Coach: Like, player development, but… Man, I think technology's always…

186
00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:14.490
Coach: getting better, and I think they're finding different ways to measure things that…

187
00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:23.010
Coach: I would think in the future, yeah, I mean, it's even, like, whether it's your stroke differential, or all these different rankings, and…

188
00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:30.609
Coach: I mean, I would think technology has to get better and keep improving, it's just they're rewriting the codes to…

189
00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:35.919
Coach: analyze the data, right? That's… did you play on a tough golf course? I mean, I think…

190
00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:42.389
Coach: you know, I think the USGA is even doing it now, how, like, they changed the rating…

191
00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:47.839
Coach: I don't… I think I'm saying this right, but you could correct me, or you should ask him, it's like.

192
00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.720
Coach: Like, even the membership handicap is being variable by the day.

193
00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:54.560
Coach: You know, like… Yeah.

194
00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:59.519
Coach: If it's a… well, and I think even over, like, in Scotland, they almost, like…

195
00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:13.609
Coach: I want to say, like, they changed the difficulty of the course per day, because, you know, if you're… I mean, your scoring average in a rainy and windy day is not going to be the same as if it's summer and clear and…

196
00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.640
Coach: You know, so I think it's more like…

197
00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:19.689
Coach: it against the competition of that day, does that make sense? Like…

198
00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.370
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, that definitely does.

199
00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:26.470
Coach: So, I mean, I think technology definitely has to get better. I mean, if it wasn't, why would you be doing this project?

200
00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.819
Coach: And if you're not thinking the techno… I mean, I think that's…

201
00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:37.739
Coach: I think what's hard with golf is it's just, like, an old sport that's been around forever, but now…

202
00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:48.229
Coach: you know, that's why I think everyone hits it so far and plays so well. I mean, I think you gotta… you gotta start… everyone complains about the ball, but I think you gotta make the drivers smaller.

203
00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:54.940
Coach: I mean, the heads are too big, that's why you hit it so… waiting so long?

204
00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:56.440
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

205
00:20:57.260 --> 00:21:06.760
Natalie Spiska: I definitely, I've kept on to my Callaway driver for a good 6 years now, just because I… I don't like the bigger heads, I want it to stay small, so I definitely agree with you on that.

206
00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:14.279
Coach: Yeah, but I think you almost need to try a new one. I think these faces and the weighting, it's surprising that you're not changing yourself, but it just keeps getting further.

207
00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:21.780
Natalie Spiska: I mean, I think the shaft on your driver's the most important piece, because it just doesn't matter what's at the end of the club head if you deliver it wrong.

208
00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:25.480
Coach: Yeah. So keep the same shaft, but just try a new head.

211
00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:40.090
Natalie Spiska: And my final question, overall, would you say that technology has had a positive or negative impact on your program?

212
00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:47.989
Coach: Oh, totally positive. I mean, it's like… I think it's just streamlining or fast-tracking it, like, instead of…

213
00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:58.500
Coach: you know, the data is… makes it easy to show even a player, like, this is what you're doing, this is why it's going there, like, I think it gives you the answers to the test.

214
00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:01.720
Natalie Spiska: That sounds good.

215
00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:07.450
Coach: But I think you gotta be a little bit of an expert, like, I think what's hard is, like, even the trackman.

216
00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:15.199
Coach: not put it on him, but I don't… I doubt your coach knows about path and angle of attack, you know, like… you know, we break [Coach]

217
00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:16.960
Natalie Spiska: I know somewhat, he's learning.

218
00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:21.220
Coach: He's learning, yeah, he's trying to put the key in the car, it's a push-button start, you know?

219
00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:27.930
Coach: But, don't worry, I know your coach well, you can tell I'm breaking his jobs.

220
00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:33.029
Natalie Spiska: No worries. I told him that I was interviewing you today, and he got very excited.